---
import Page from '../../layouts/Page.astro';
import ScoreHistory from '../../components/ScoreHistory.astro';
import SharedResults from '../../components/SharedResults.astro';
import NasaLeanTestInterpretation from '../../components/interpretation/NasaLeanTest.astro';
import { FAQ, FAQ_ORDER } from '../../tools/nasa-lean-test.content';
import { toolJsonLd } from '../../tools/jsonld';

const jsonLd = toolJsonLd('NASA Lean Test', '/tools/nasa-lean-test/', FAQ_ORDER.map(k => FAQ[k]));
---

<Page
	title="NASA lean test: free at-home tilt table test with timer"
	description="Do the NASA lean test (the poor man's tilt table test) at home with a guided timer and heart rate logging at each stage. Free and interactive, with your orthostatic heart rate change calculated and the POTS thresholds explained."
>
	<Fragment slot="head">
		<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(jsonLd)} />
	</Fragment>

			<!-- ─── SETUP SCREEN ─────────────────────────────────────────── -->
			<div id="screen-setup" class="screen">
				<div class="tool-header">
					<a href="/tools/" class="section-label tools">Tools</a>
					<h1>NASA Lean Test</h1>
					<p class="subtitle">Orthostatic Intolerance Protocol</p>
					<div class="disclaimer">
						<strong>This is not a diagnostic tool.</strong> The NASA Lean Test can provide useful information to discuss with your doctor, but it cannot diagnose POTS, orthostatic hypotension, or any other condition. Stop the test immediately if you feel faint, unwell, or develop worsening symptoms. All results should be discussed with a clinician.
					</div>
				</div>

				<div class="setup-content">
					<h2>What this test does</h2>
					<p>The NASA lean test is a simplified version of a tilt table test that you can perform at home with just a heart rate monitor or a finger on your pulse. It is sometimes called the “poor man’s tilt table test” and is widely used in POTS and dysautonomia communities as a practical screening method for orthostatic intolerance.</p>
<p>The test involves lying flat for a period, then standing up and leaning against a wall with your heels a few inches from the wall and your back supported. Your heart rate is recorded at intervals while lying and while standing. The key finding that suggests POTS is whether heart rate rises by 30 or more beats per minute within 10 minutes of standing (40 or more at ages 12 to 19) without a significant drop in blood pressure. Some definitions also accept a standing heart rate above 120 bpm.</p>
<p>A formal tilt table test involves being strapped to a motorised table in a clinical setting, which can be difficult to access, especially through the NHS where waiting times for autonomic testing are often long. The NASA lean test is not a replacement for formal testing, but it gives you a structured way to gather objective data at home that you can bring to appointments. Many patients find that presenting lean test results helps move conversations forward with clinicians who may not otherwise consider autonomic testing.</p>
<p>This guide walks you through the test step by step, with an interactive timer for each stage and fields to log your heart rate readings. You can repeat it on different days to build up a picture of your orthostatic heart rate response. To put a number on symptoms as well as heart rate, complete the <a href="/tools/vanderbilt-orthostatic-symptom-score/">Vanderbilt Orthostatic Symptom Score</a> in the final minute of standing; it is the symptom score POTS trials use at exactly that point. For how the lean test fits alongside symptom questionnaires when you are wondering whether you have POTS, see <a href="/testing/do-i-have-pots/">Do I have POTS?</a></p>

					<h2>What you need</h2>
					<ul>
						<li><strong>Heart rate monitor:</strong> a pulse oximeter, smartwatch, or heart rate monitor. You need to be able to read your heart rate quickly at the prompt.</li>
						<li><strong>Blood pressure cuff</strong> (optional but useful): a standard upper-arm cuff. If you don't have one, simply leave the BP fields blank.</li>
						<li><strong>A smooth wall to lean against.</strong></li>
						<li><strong>Somewhere comfortable to lie flat:</strong> a bed, sofa, or mat.</li>
						<li><strong>Your device propped up</strong> so you can see the screen while lying down and while standing.</li>
					</ul>

					<h2>How to position yourself</h2>
					<div class="position-guide">
						<div class="position-item">
							<div class="position-icon" aria-hidden="true">—</div>
							<div>
								<strong>Supine phase</strong><br>
								Lie flat on your back. Arms at your sides or resting gently on your abdomen. Stay still and as relaxed as possible. Avoid a pillow if you can manage without one.
							</div>
						</div>
						<div class="position-item">
							<div class="position-icon" aria-hidden="true">|</div>
							<div>
								<strong>Standing/leaning phase</strong><br>
								Stand with your back flat against a smooth wall. Move your feet forward until they are approximately <strong>15–20 cm (6–8 inches)</strong> from the wall. Your legs should be straight and your weight through your heels. Keep your arms loose at your sides. This removes active leg-muscle use from the test, making it a closer approximation to passive tilt.
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>

					<h2>Before you start</h2>
					<ul>
						<li>Avoid a large meal, caffeine, or exercise for at least 2 hours beforehand.</li>
						<li>Make sure someone is nearby or can check on you if you have a history of fainting.</li>
						<li>Have water to hand.</li>
						<li>You will be prompted for readings at <strong>1, 3, 5, and 10 minutes</strong> in each phase. An audio chime and visual cue will alert you; you do not need to watch the screen continuously.</li>
						<li>A <strong>Stop test</strong> button is always visible. Use it if you feel unwell, then sit or lie down immediately.</li>
					</ul>

					<button id="start-btn" class="btn-primary btn-large">Begin test</button>
				</div>
			</div>

			<!-- ─── TIMER SCREEN (shared for both phases) ────────────────── -->
			<div id="screen-timer" class="screen" hidden>
				<div class="phase-header">
					<span id="phase-label" class="phase-badge">Supine phase</span>
					<button id="stop-btn" class="btn-stop">Stop test</button>
				</div>

				<div id="timer-display" class="timer-display">
					<div id="timer-value" class="timer-value">10:00</div>
					<div class="timer-label">remaining</div>
				</div>

				<div class="phase-status">
					<div id="next-reading-wrapper" class="next-reading">
						Next reading in <strong id="next-reading-time">1:00</strong>
					</div>
					<div class="readings-count"><span id="readings-done">0</span>/4 readings recorded</div>
				</div>

				<div class="live-table-wrapper">
					<table class="live-table">
						<thead>
							<tr><th>Time</th><th>HR (bpm)</th><th>Systolic</th><th>Diastolic</th></tr>
						</thead>
						<tbody>
							<tr><td>1 min</td><td id="live-hr-1" class="reading-cell">—</td><td id="live-sys-1" class="reading-cell">—</td><td id="live-dia-1" class="reading-cell">—</td></tr>
							<tr><td>3 min</td><td id="live-hr-3" class="reading-cell">—</td><td id="live-sys-3" class="reading-cell">—</td><td id="live-dia-3" class="reading-cell">—</td></tr>
							<tr><td>5 min</td><td id="live-hr-5" class="reading-cell">—</td><td id="live-sys-5" class="reading-cell">—</td><td id="live-dia-5" class="reading-cell">—</td></tr>
							<tr><td>10 min</td><td id="live-hr-10" class="reading-cell">—</td><td id="live-sys-10" class="reading-cell">—</td><td id="live-dia-10" class="reading-cell">—</td></tr>
						</tbody>
					</table>
				</div>
			</div>

			<!-- ─── READING PROMPT OVERLAY ───────────────────────────────── -->
			<div id="prompt-overlay" class="overlay" hidden aria-modal="true" role="dialog">
				<div class="overlay-card">
					<div class="overlay-heading">
						<div class="overlay-badge">Reading time</div>
						<h2 id="prompt-time-label" class="overlay-title">1 minute</h2>
					</div>
					<p class="overlay-instruction">Take your reading now and enter it below. The timer is still running.</p>

					<div class="input-group">
						<label for="input-hr">Heart rate <span class="unit">bpm</span> <span class="required">required</span></label>
						<input type="number" id="input-hr" min="20" max="300" placeholder="e.g. 72" inputmode="numeric" autocomplete="off" />
					</div>

					<div class="input-group">
						<label>Blood pressure <span class="unit">mmHg</span> <span class="optional">optional</span></label>
						<div class="bp-row">
							<input type="number" id="input-sys" min="40" max="260" placeholder="Systolic" inputmode="numeric" autocomplete="off" aria-label="Systolic blood pressure" />
							<span class="bp-sep" aria-hidden="true">/</span>
							<input type="number" id="input-dia" min="20" max="160" placeholder="Diastolic" inputmode="numeric" autocomplete="off" aria-label="Diastolic blood pressure" />
						</div>
					</div>

					<p id="input-error" class="input-error" hidden>Please enter your heart rate before saving.</p>

					<div class="overlay-actions">
						<button id="save-reading-btn" class="btn-primary">Save reading</button>
						<button id="skip-reading-btn" class="btn-skip">Skip this reading</button>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>

			<!-- ─── SUPINE SYMPTOMS SCREEN ───────────────────────────────── -->
			<div id="screen-supine-symptoms" class="screen" hidden>
				<div class="screen-content">
					<h2>Supine phase complete</h2>
					<p>Before you stand up, note any symptoms you experienced during the lying phase. Then press continue.</p>

					<div class="input-group">
						<label for="supine-symptoms-text">Symptoms during lying phase <span class="optional">optional</span></label>
						<textarea id="supine-symptoms-text" rows="3" placeholder="e.g. No symptoms, or: mild headache, heart pounding, breathlessness"></textarea>
					</div>

					<div class="input-group">
						<label for="supine-severity">Overall symptom severity <span class="unit">0 = none, 10 = severe</span></label>
						<div class="severity-row">
							<input type="range" id="supine-severity" min="0" max="10" value="0" />
							<span id="supine-severity-value" class="severity-number">0</span>
						</div>
					</div>

					<button id="go-transition-btn" class="btn-primary btn-large">Continue to standing phase</button>
				</div>
			</div>

			<!-- ─── TRANSITION SCREEN ────────────────────────────────────── -->
			<div id="screen-transition" class="screen" hidden>
				<div class="screen-content">
					<h2>Now stand up and lean</h2>

					<div class="steps">
						<div class="step">
							<span class="step-num">1</span>
							<p>Move to a smooth wall. Stand with your back flat against it.</p>
						</div>
						<div class="step">
							<span class="step-num">2</span>
							<p>Slide your feet forward until they are approximately <strong>15–20 cm (6–8 inches)</strong> from the wall. Keep your legs straight and your weight through your heels.</p>
						</div>
						<div class="step">
							<span class="step-num">3</span>
							<p>Rest your arms loosely at your sides. Try to stay relaxed. Avoid tensing your leg muscles.</p>
						</div>
						<div class="step">
							<span class="step-num">4</span>
							<p>If you feel faint or significantly worse at any point, press <strong>Stop test</strong> and sit or lie down immediately.</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<p class="transition-note">When you are in position, press the button below. The 10-minute standing timer will start immediately.</p>

					<button id="ready-standing-btn" class="btn-primary btn-large">I'm in position: start standing phase</button>
				</div>
			</div>

			<!-- ─── STANDING SYMPTOMS SCREEN ─────────────────────────────── -->
			<div id="screen-standing-symptoms" class="screen" hidden>
				<div class="screen-content">
					<h2>Standing phase complete</h2>
					<p>You can sit or lie down now. Note any symptoms you experienced during the standing phase.</p>

					<div class="input-group">
						<label for="standing-symptoms-text">Symptoms during standing phase <span class="optional">optional</span></label>
						<textarea id="standing-symptoms-text" rows="3" placeholder="e.g. Dizziness, palpitations, breathlessness, nausea, chest tightness"></textarea>
					</div>

					<div class="input-group">
						<label for="standing-severity">Overall symptom severity <span class="unit">0 = none, 10 = severe</span></label>
						<div class="severity-row">
							<input type="range" id="standing-severity" min="0" max="10" value="0" />
							<span id="standing-severity-value" class="severity-number">0</span>
						</div>
					</div>

					<button id="go-results-btn" class="btn-primary btn-large">View results</button>
				</div>
			</div>

			<!-- ─── RESULTS SCREEN ───────────────────────────────────────── -->
			<div id="screen-results" class="screen" hidden>
				<div class="results-content">
					<h2>Your results</h2>
					<p id="stopped-note" class="stopped-note" hidden>Note: test was stopped before completion. Results are based on data collected up to that point.</p>

					<div id="summary-cards" class="summary-cards"></div>

					<div class="results-tables">
						<div class="results-table-block">
							<h3>Supine (lying) phase</h3>
							<table class="results-table">
								<thead><tr><th>Time</th><th>HR (bpm)</th><th>BP (sys/dia)</th></tr></thead>
								<tbody id="results-supine-body"></tbody>
							</table>
							<p id="results-supine-symptoms" class="symptom-note"></p>
						</div>
						<div class="results-table-block">
							<h3>Standing (leaning) phase</h3>
							<table class="results-table">
								<thead><tr><th>Time</th><th>HR (bpm)</th><th>BP (sys/dia)</th></tr></thead>
								<tbody id="results-standing-body"></tbody>
							</table>
							<p id="results-standing-symptoms" class="symptom-note"></p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<h3>Interpretation</h3>
					<div id="results-interpretation" class="interpretation-box"></div>

					<div class="threshold-box">
						<h4>Reference thresholds</h4>
						<ul>
							<!-- REVIEW: thresholds rewritten to match Sheldon 2015 and Vernino 2021; see nasa-lean-test.content.ts. -->
							<li><strong>POTS:</strong> A sustained heart rate increase of 30 bpm or more within 10 minutes of standing or tilt (40 bpm or more at ages 12 to 19), without orthostatic hypotension, with symptoms on standing for at least 3 months. Some definitions also accept a standing heart rate above 120 bpm.</li>
							<li><strong>Orthostatic hypotension:</strong> A drop in systolic BP of 20 mmHg or more, or diastolic BP of 10 mmHg or more, within 3 minutes of standing (the definition used in lean test research).</li>
							<li><strong>Note on this test:</strong> The NASA lean test uses a wall lean rather than a true stand or a passive tilt, and it has not been validated against either. These thresholds were set for standing and tilt tests. Results should always be interpreted alongside symptoms and clinical context.</li>
						</ul>
					</div>

					<div class="results-disclaimer">
						<strong>This is not a diagnostic tool.</strong> These results are intended to help you have a more informed conversation with your doctor. A single test does not establish or rule out any diagnosis. Discuss all results with a clinician.
					</div>

					<ScoreHistory toolId="nasa-lean-test" toolName="NASA lean test" />

					<div class="export-buttons">
						<button id="copy-btn" class="btn-secondary">Copy results as text</button>
						<button id="print-btn" class="btn-secondary">Print / save as PDF</button>
						<button id="restart-btn" class="btn-outline">Start a new test</button>
					</div>
					<p id="copy-confirm" class="copy-confirm" hidden>Results copied to clipboard.</p>
				</div>
			</div>

			<SharedResults toolId="nasa-lean-test" />

			<NasaLeanTestInterpretation />

</Page>

<script>
import { nasaLeanTest } from '../../tools/nasa-lean-test';
import { mountScoreHistory, mountSharedResults } from '../../scripts/results/scoreHistory';

const history = mountScoreHistory(nasaLeanTest);
mountSharedResults(nasaLeanTest);

const PROMPT_SECONDS = [60, 180, 300, 600];
const PHASE_DURATION = 600;

const testData = {
	supine:   { readings: {}, symptoms: '', severity: 0 },
	standing: { readings: {}, symptoms: '', severity: 0 },
	stoppedEarly: false,
};

let currentPhase = 'supine';
let elapsed = 0;
let timerInterval = null;
let activePromptSec = null;
let pendingPrompts = [];
let handledPrompts = new Set();
let audioCtx = null;

// ── Audio ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
function playChime() {
	try {
		if (!audioCtx) audioCtx = new (window.AudioContext || window.webkitAudioContext)();
		[[523.25, 0], [659.25, 0.18]].forEach(([freq, delay]) => {
			const osc = audioCtx.createOscillator();
			const gain = audioCtx.createGain();
			osc.connect(gain); gain.connect(audioCtx.destination);
			osc.type = 'sine';
			osc.frequency.setValueAtTime(freq, audioCtx.currentTime + delay);
			gain.gain.setValueAtTime(0.35, audioCtx.currentTime + delay);
			gain.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.001, audioCtx.currentTime + delay + 0.7);
			osc.start(audioCtx.currentTime + delay);
			osc.stop(audioCtx.currentTime + delay + 0.7);
		});
	} catch (_) { /* silently skip if audio blocked */ }
	const d = document.getElementById('timer-display');
	d?.classList.add('flash');
	setTimeout(() => d?.classList.remove('flash'), 700);
}

// ── Utilities ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
function fmt(s) {
	return `${Math.floor(s / 60)}:${String(s % 60).padStart(2, '0')}`;
}

function show(id) {
	document.querySelectorAll('.screen').forEach(el => el.hidden = true);
	document.getElementById(id).hidden = false;
	window.scrollTo(0, 0);
}

function minuteKey(sec) {
	return sec === 60 ? 1 : sec === 180 ? 3 : sec === 300 ? 5 : 10;
}

function minuteLabel(sec) {
	return sec === 60 ? '1 minute' : sec === 180 ? '3 minutes' : sec === 300 ? '5 minutes' : '10 minutes';
}

// ── Timer ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
function startTimer() {
	elapsed = 0;
	handledPrompts.clear();
	pendingPrompts = [];
	activePromptSec = null;
	updateTimer();
	timerInterval = setInterval(tick, 1000);
}

function tick() {
	elapsed = Math.min(elapsed + 1, PHASE_DURATION);
	updateTimer();
	checkPrompts();
	if (elapsed >= PHASE_DURATION && activePromptSec === null && handledPrompts.has(600)) {
		clearInterval(timerInterval);
		endPhase();
	}
}

function stopTimer() {
	clearInterval(timerInterval);
	timerInterval = null;
}

function updateTimer() {
	const remaining = Math.max(0, PHASE_DURATION - elapsed);
	document.getElementById('timer-value').textContent = fmt(remaining);

	const next = PROMPT_SECONDS.find(t => !handledPrompts.has(t));
	const wrapper = document.getElementById('next-reading-wrapper');
	if (next && next > elapsed) {
		wrapper.hidden = false;
		document.getElementById('next-reading-time').textContent = fmt(next - elapsed);
	} else {
		wrapper.hidden = true;
	}

	document.getElementById('readings-done').textContent = String(handledPrompts.size);
}

function checkPrompts() {
	for (const t of PROMPT_SECONDS) {
		if (elapsed >= t && !handledPrompts.has(t)) {
			if (activePromptSec === null) {
				showPrompt(t);
			} else if (!pendingPrompts.includes(t)) {
				pendingPrompts.push(t);
			}
		}
	}
}

// ── Prompt overlay ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
function showPrompt(sec) {
	activePromptSec = sec;
	playChime();
	document.getElementById('prompt-time-label').textContent = minuteLabel(sec);
	document.getElementById('input-hr').value = '';
	document.getElementById('input-sys').value = '';
	document.getElementById('input-dia').value = '';
	document.getElementById('input-error').hidden = true;
	document.getElementById('prompt-overlay').hidden = false;
	setTimeout(() => document.getElementById('input-hr').focus(), 80);
}

function closePrompt() {
	document.getElementById('prompt-overlay').hidden = true;
	const next = pendingPrompts.shift();
	if (next !== undefined) {
		showPrompt(next);
	} else {
		activePromptSec = null;
		if (elapsed >= PHASE_DURATION) {
			stopTimer();
			endPhase();
		}
	}
}

function saveReading() {
	const hrEl = document.getElementById('input-hr');
	const sysEl = document.getElementById('input-sys');
	const diaEl = document.getElementById('input-dia');
	const hr = parseInt(hrEl.value);

	if (!hrEl.value || isNaN(hr) || hr < 20 || hr > 300) {
		document.getElementById('input-error').hidden = false;
		hrEl.focus();
		return;
	}

	const sys = sysEl.value ? parseInt(sysEl.value) : null;
	const dia = diaEl.value ? parseInt(diaEl.value) : null;
	const mk = minuteKey(activePromptSec);

	testData[currentPhase].readings[mk] = { hr, sys, dia };
	handledPrompts.add(activePromptSec);

	// Update live table cells
	document.getElementById(`live-hr-${mk}`).textContent = String(hr);
	document.getElementById(`live-sys-${mk}`).textContent = sys != null ? String(sys) : '—';
	document.getElementById(`live-dia-${mk}`).textContent = dia != null ? String(dia) : '—';

	closePrompt();
}

function skipReading() {
	handledPrompts.add(activePromptSec);
	closePrompt();
}

// ── Phase flow ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
function endPhase() {
	show(currentPhase === 'supine' ? 'screen-supine-symptoms' : 'screen-standing-symptoms');
}

function stopEarly() {
	stopTimer();
	document.getElementById('prompt-overlay').hidden = true;
	testData.stoppedEarly = true;
	endPhase();
}

function startPhase(phase) {
	currentPhase = phase;
	document.getElementById('phase-label').textContent =
		phase === 'supine' ? 'Supine phase (lying)' : 'Standing phase (leaning)';
	['1','3','5','10'].forEach(t => {
		['hr','sys','dia'].forEach(k => {
			document.getElementById(`live-${k}-${t}`).textContent = '—';
		});
	});
	show('screen-timer');
	startTimer();
}

// ── Results ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
function getLastHR(phase) {
	const r = testData[phase].readings;
	return r[10]?.hr ?? r[5]?.hr ?? r[3]?.hr ?? r[1]?.hr ?? null;
}

function getPeakStandingHR() {
	let peak = null, peakMin = null;
	for (const t of [1,3,5,10]) {
		const hr = testData.standing.readings[t]?.hr;
		if (hr != null && (peak === null || hr > peak)) { peak = hr; peakMin = t; }
	}
	return { hr: peak, min: peakMin };
}

function getMinStandingBP() {
	let sys = null, dia = null;
	for (const t of [1,3,5,10]) {
		const r = testData.standing.readings[t];
		if (r?.sys != null && (sys === null || r.sys < sys)) sys = r.sys;
		if (r?.dia != null && (dia === null || r.dia < dia)) dia = r.dia;
	}
	return { sys, dia };
}

function fillResultsTable(phase) {
	const tbody = document.getElementById(`results-${phase}-body`);
	tbody.innerHTML = '';
	for (const t of [1,3,5,10]) {
		const r = testData[phase].readings[t];
		const hr = r?.hr != null ? r.hr : '—';
		const bp = (r?.sys != null && r?.dia != null) ? `${r.sys}/${r.dia}`
		         : r?.sys != null ? `${r.sys}/—` : '—';
		tbody.innerHTML += `<tr><td>${t} min</td><td>${hr}</td><td>${bp}</td></tr>`;
	}
}

function showResults() {
	show('screen-results');

	if (testData.stoppedEarly) {
		document.getElementById('stopped-note').hidden = false;
	}

	fillResultsTable('supine');
	fillResultsTable('standing');

	const ssEl = document.getElementById('results-supine-symptoms');
	const d = testData.supine;
	ssEl.textContent = `Symptom severity (supine): ${d.severity}/10${d.symptoms ? '. ' + d.symptoms : ''}`;

	const stEl = document.getElementById('results-standing-symptoms');
	const ds = testData.standing;
	stEl.textContent = `Symptom severity (standing): ${ds.severity}/10${ds.symptoms ? '. ' + ds.symptoms : ''}`;

	const finalSupineHR = getLastHR('supine');
	const { hr: peakHR, min: peakMin } = getPeakStandingHR();
	const hrIncrease = (finalSupineHR != null && peakHR != null) ? peakHR - finalSupineHR : null;
	const finalSupineSys = testData.supine.readings[10]?.sys ?? testData.supine.readings[5]?.sys
	                     ?? testData.supine.readings[3]?.sys ?? testData.supine.readings[1]?.sys ?? null;
	const finalSupineDia = testData.supine.readings[10]?.dia ?? testData.supine.readings[5]?.dia
	                     ?? testData.supine.readings[3]?.dia ?? testData.supine.readings[1]?.dia ?? null;
	const { sys: minStandSys, dia: minStandDia } = getMinStandingBP();
	const sysDrop = (finalSupineSys != null && minStandSys != null) ? finalSupineSys - minStandSys : null;
	const diaDrop = (finalSupineDia != null && minStandDia != null) ? finalSupineDia - minStandDia : null;

	// Summary cards
	const cards = document.getElementById('summary-cards');
	cards.innerHTML = '';

	if (hrIncrease != null) {
		const flagged = hrIncrease >= 30;
		cards.innerHTML += `
			<div class="summary-card${flagged ? ' card-flagged' : ''}">
				<div class="card-value">${hrIncrease >= 0 ? '+' : ''}${hrIncrease} bpm</div>
				<div class="card-label">Heart rate increase on standing</div>
				<div class="card-detail">From ${finalSupineHR} bpm (final supine) to ${peakHR} bpm peak at ${peakMin} min standing</div>
			</div>`;
	}
	if (peakHR != null) {
		const flagged = peakHR > 120;
		cards.innerHTML += `
			<div class="summary-card${flagged ? ' card-flagged' : ''}">
				<div class="card-value">${peakHR} bpm</div>
				<div class="card-label">Peak standing heart rate</div>
				<div class="card-detail">Recorded at ${peakMin} minute${peakMin !== 1 ? 's' : ''} of standing</div>
			</div>`;
	}
	if (sysDrop != null) {
		const flagged = sysDrop >= 20;
		cards.innerHTML += `
			<div class="summary-card${flagged ? ' card-flagged' : ''}">
				<div class="card-value">${sysDrop > 0 ? '−' : '+'}${Math.abs(sysDrop)} mmHg</div>
				<div class="card-label">Systolic BP change on standing</div>
				<div class="card-detail">From ${finalSupineSys} mmHg (supine) to ${minStandSys} mmHg (lowest standing)</div>
			</div>`;
	}

	// Interpretation
	const interp = document.getElementById('results-interpretation');
	const hasOH = (sysDrop != null && sysDrop >= 20) || (diaDrop != null && diaDrop >= 10);
	const hasPOTS = hrIncrease != null && (hrIncrease >= 30 || (peakHR != null && peakHR > 120));
	const hasData = peakHR != null;

	let html = '';
	if (!hasData) {
		html = '<p>No standing readings were recorded, so no interpretation is possible.</p>';
	} else if (hasOH) {
		html = `<p><strong>Blood pressure pattern:</strong> Your results show a drop in blood pressure on standing that meets the threshold for orthostatic hypotension (systolic drop ≥20 mmHg or diastolic drop ≥10 mmHg). Orthostatic hypotension is a distinct condition from POTS and is managed differently. Discuss these results with your doctor.</p>`;
		if (hasPOTS) {
			html += `<p><strong>Heart rate pattern:</strong> Your results also show a heart rate increase that meets one of the commonly referenced thresholds. When orthostatic hypotension and tachycardia co-occur, clinical assessment is needed to interpret the picture.</p>`;
		}
	} else if (hasPOTS) {
		html = `<p><strong>Heart rate pattern:</strong> `;
		if (hrIncrease != null && hrIncrease >= 30) html += `Your heart rate increased by ${hrIncrease} bpm on standing. `;
		if (peakHR > 120) html += `Your peak standing heart rate was ${peakHR} bpm. `;
		html += `Your readings meet one or more of the heart rate thresholds used in POTS definitions (a rise of 30 bpm or more, or 40 bpm or more at ages 12 to 19; some definitions also accept a standing rate above 120 bpm). This home test cannot establish a diagnosis: it has not been validated against clinical testing, some healthy people also pass 30 bpm on a lean test, and a diagnosis also needs symptoms for at least 3 months with other causes ruled out. Discuss these results with your doctor.</p>`;
		if (sysDrop != null) {
			html += `<p><strong>Blood pressure:</strong> No orthostatic hypotension was identified (systolic drop was ${sysDrop} mmHg, below the 20 mmHg threshold).</p>`;
		}
	} else {
		html = `<p><strong>Heart rate pattern:</strong> `;
		if (hrIncrease != null) html += `Your heart rate increased by ${hrIncrease} bpm on standing. This does not meet the 30 bpm threshold used in POTS definitions. `;
		if (peakHR != null) html += `Your peak standing heart rate was ${peakHR} bpm. `;
		html += `If you have significant symptoms of orthostatic intolerance, discuss them with your doctor regardless of this result. A sub-threshold rise can still cause symptoms and may warrant further investigation.</p>`;
		if (sysDrop != null) {
			html += `<p><strong>Blood pressure:</strong> No orthostatic hypotension was identified (systolic drop was ${sysDrop} mmHg).</p>`;
		}
	}
	interp.innerHTML = html;

	if (hrIncrease != null) {
		const subscores: Record<string, number> = { supinehr: finalSupineHR, peakhr: peakHR, supinesymptoms: d.severity, standingsymptoms: ds.severity };
		if (sysDrop != null) subscores.sysdrop = sysDrop;
		if (diaDrop != null) subscores.diadrop = diaDrop;
		const bpText = sysDrop != null ? `, systolic BP change ${sysDrop > 0 ? '-' : '+'}${Math.abs(sysDrop)} mmHg` : '';
		history.record({
			total: hrIncrease,
			subscores,
			summary: `NASA lean test: heart rate rise ${hrIncrease} bpm (${finalSupineHR} supine to ${peakHR} peak standing)${bpText}${testData.stoppedEarly ? ', stopped early' : ''}`,
		});
	}
}

// ── Export ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
function buildText() {
	const date = new Date().toLocaleDateString('en-GB', { day: 'numeric', month: 'long', year: 'numeric' });
	const lines = [
		'NASA LEAN TEST RESULTS',
		`Date: ${date}`,
		'Source: Post Viral Recovery, postviralrecovery.com',
		'═'.repeat(45),
		'',
		'SUPINE PHASE (lying)',
		'─'.repeat(25),
	];
	for (const t of [1,3,5,10]) {
		const r = testData.supine.readings[t];
		if (r) {
			const bp = (r.sys && r.dia) ? `  BP: ${r.sys}/${r.dia} mmHg` : '';
			lines.push(`${t} min:  HR: ${r.hr} bpm${bp}`);
		} else {
			lines.push(`${t} min:  Not recorded`);
		}
	}
	lines.push(`Symptoms: ${testData.supine.symptoms || 'None noted'}`);
	lines.push(`Severity: ${testData.supine.severity}/10`);
	lines.push('');
	lines.push('STANDING PHASE (leaning against wall)');
	lines.push('─'.repeat(25));
	for (const t of [1,3,5,10]) {
		const r = testData.standing.readings[t];
		if (r) {
			const bp = (r.sys && r.dia) ? `  BP: ${r.sys}/${r.dia} mmHg` : '';
			lines.push(`${t} min:  HR: ${r.hr} bpm${bp}`);
		} else {
			lines.push(`${t} min:  Not recorded`);
		}
	}
	lines.push(`Symptoms: ${testData.standing.symptoms || 'None noted'}`);
	lines.push(`Severity: ${testData.standing.severity}/10`);
	lines.push('');

	const finalSupineHR = getLastHR('supine');
	const { hr: peakHR, min: peakMin } = getPeakStandingHR();
	lines.push('KEY FIGURES');
	lines.push('─'.repeat(25));
	if (finalSupineHR != null) lines.push(`Final supine HR:     ${finalSupineHR} bpm`);
	if (peakHR != null)        lines.push(`Peak standing HR:    ${peakHR} bpm (at ${peakMin} min)`);
	if (finalSupineHR != null && peakHR != null) {
		lines.push(`HR increase:         ${peakHR - finalSupineHR} bpm`);
	}
	lines.push('');
	lines.push('═'.repeat(45));
	lines.push('This is an informational tool only. Results should be discussed with a clinician.');
	lines.push('POTS threshold: sustained rise of 30 bpm or more within 10 minutes (40 bpm at ages 12-19), no orthostatic hypotension, symptoms for 3 months or more; some definitions also accept standing HR >120 bpm');
	lines.push('Orthostatic hypotension threshold: systolic drop ≥20 mmHg or diastolic drop ≥10 mmHg');
	return lines.join('\n');
}

// ── Event wiring ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
document.getElementById('start-btn').addEventListener('click', () => {
	// Initialise AudioContext on first user interaction (iOS requirement)
	if (!audioCtx) {
		try { audioCtx = new (window.AudioContext || window.webkitAudioContext)(); } catch (_) {}
	}
	startPhase('supine');
});

document.getElementById('stop-btn').addEventListener('click', stopEarly);
document.getElementById('save-reading-btn').addEventListener('click', saveReading);
document.getElementById('skip-reading-btn').addEventListener('click', skipReading);

document.getElementById('input-hr').addEventListener('keydown', e => {
	if (e.key === 'Enter') saveReading();
});

document.getElementById('go-transition-btn').addEventListener('click', () => {
	testData.supine.symptoms = document.getElementById('supine-symptoms-text').value.trim();
	testData.supine.severity = parseInt(document.getElementById('supine-severity').value);
	show('screen-transition');
});

document.getElementById('ready-standing-btn').addEventListener('click', () => {
	startPhase('standing');
});

document.getElementById('go-results-btn').addEventListener('click', () => {
	testData.standing.symptoms = document.getElementById('standing-symptoms-text').value.trim();
	testData.standing.severity = parseInt(document.getElementById('standing-severity').value);
	showResults();
});

document.getElementById('supine-severity').addEventListener('input', function() {
	document.getElementById('supine-severity-value').textContent = this.value;
});
document.getElementById('standing-severity').addEventListener('input', function() {
	document.getElementById('standing-severity-value').textContent = this.value;
});

document.getElementById('copy-btn').addEventListener('click', () => {
	navigator.clipboard.writeText(buildText()).then(() => {
		const el = document.getElementById('copy-confirm');
		el.hidden = false;
		setTimeout(() => el.hidden = true, 3000);
	});
});

document.getElementById('print-btn').addEventListener('click', () => window.print());

document.getElementById('restart-btn').addEventListener('click', () => {
	// A new test is a new result, not an edit of the one just saved.
	history.startNew();
	testData.supine   = { readings: {}, symptoms: '', severity: 0 };
	testData.standing = { readings: {}, symptoms: '', severity: 0 };
	testData.stoppedEarly = false;
	document.getElementById('stopped-note').hidden = true;
	document.getElementById('supine-symptoms-text').value = '';
	document.getElementById('standing-symptoms-text').value = '';
	document.getElementById('supine-severity').value = '0';
	document.getElementById('standing-severity').value = '0';
	document.getElementById('supine-severity-value').textContent = '0';
	document.getElementById('standing-severity-value').textContent = '0';
	show('screen-setup');
});
</script>

